1
00:00:00,917 --> 00:00:04,045
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:15,306
<i>You won't support any other</i>
<i>candidate? Just Arnaldo?</i>

3
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>You can count on me, Congressman.</i>

4
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,643
<i>There's no turning back, Ivy.</i>

5
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:21,855
<i>I may be far away,</i>
<i>but you have my full support.</i>

6
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:24,733
<i>Now's the time to establish</i>
<i>a new government.</i>

7
00:00:24,816 --> 00:00:26,985
<i>A government that will truly understand</i>

8
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:28,820
<i>the problems of its people.</i>

9
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:30,613
<i>A new Ardiente!</i>

10
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,866
-<i>Long live Diego!</i>
-[all] <i>Long live Diego!</i>

11
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:35,368
<i>As your next governor,</i>

12
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:38,246
<i>I promise you that we will take this town</i>

13
00:00:38,329 --> 00:00:40,582
-<i>to even greater heights.</i>
-[applause]

14
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:44,419
<i>I want you to support my bid for governor.</i>

15
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:45,754
<i>Why would I lend you money?</i>

16
00:00:45,837 --> 00:00:48,798
<i>You know my loyalty lies</i>
<i>with your son, Arnaldo.</i>

17
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:50,175
<i>Oh, really?</i>

18
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:53,470
<i>These pictures I have of you</i>
<i>say otherwise.</i>

19
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:54,596
[Ivy] <i>If I were you,</i>

20
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:58,683
<i>I'd fire your investigator.</i>
<i>You're humiliating yourself.</i>

21
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:02,937
<i>Who do you think is capable</i>
<i>of leading this town?</i>

22
00:01:03,021 --> 00:01:05,398
<i>-Aside from us, the Ardientes?</i>
<i>-Me.</i>

23
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:08,068
<i>I will run for governor</i>
<i>against you, Arnaldo.</i>

24
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,404
[crowd clamoring]

25
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:12,447
[mouthing] <i>Diego!</i>

26
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:14,866
[Arnaldo] <i>I saw you earlier.</i>
<i>You helped Diego.</i>

27
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:18,787
<i>Ow. First, we aren't together</i>
<i>for you to feel jealous.</i>

28
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,581
<i>Once you're ready to talk</i>
<i>in a calm manner,</i>

29
00:01:21,664 --> 00:01:23,750
<i>I'm sure you know where to find me.</i>

30
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:27,170
<i>What are you doing there?</i>
<i>Get out of my room!</i>

31
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,213
<i>-Do it again.</i>
<i>-I said leave--</i>

32
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:30,757
<i>No, because I will keep</i>
<i>coming back for more.</i>

33
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,802
<i>For a politician, you're quite perverted.</i>

34
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,887
<i>Be careful.</i>
<i>That might get you into trouble.</i>

35
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:39,307
<i>-Ivy, the congressman's here.</i>
<i>-May I join you?</i>

36
00:01:41,810 --> 00:01:43,645
What are you doing here, Congressman?

37
00:01:43,728 --> 00:01:46,189
We weren't expecting you.

38
00:01:46,272 --> 00:01:47,148
[Julio] Surprise!

39
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,399
Well…

40
00:01:49,651 --> 00:01:50,944
perhaps this is a bad time.

41
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:53,446
Congressman, whatever you're thinking,

42
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,533
nothing happened between me and Arnaldo.

43
00:01:56,616 --> 00:01:59,119
The truth is, he was just
about to leave, right?

44
00:02:00,662 --> 00:02:02,789
[chuckling] I was just about to say

45
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:05,416
that you two look like
you've been swimming.

46
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,460
-Mm…
-[all chuckle]

47
00:02:07,544 --> 00:02:11,464
Nevertheless, before we leave, Miss Aguas,

48
00:02:11,548 --> 00:02:12,882
I would like you to know

49
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:16,928
that whatever relationship
you have with Arnaldo,

50
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:18,138
I support it.

51
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:20,598
To be honest,

52
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:24,853
I was expecting that you'd
bring it up to the next level.

53
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:30,608
-Next level?
-Yes!

54
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:34,988
Why, do you plan on rejecting Arnaldo?

55
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,406
Grandpa.

56
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:40,451
[Julio] I won't allow Miss Aguas
to dump you just like that.

57
00:02:40,535 --> 00:02:44,873
Congressman. Are you suggesting
a shotgun wedding?

58
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:46,291
[Julio clears throat]

59
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:49,252
I hope we don't come to that.

60
00:02:49,794 --> 00:02:53,256
[tense music playing]

61
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,638
Uh…

62
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,266
Ivy, that's not what Grandpa meant.

63
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:08,062
No. Actually, that's exactly
what I mean to say.

64
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,274
You two would make a good couple.

65
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:14,444
So, why should we wait any longer?

66
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:19,991
I believe the two of you should
get engaged as soon as possible!

67
00:03:20,074 --> 00:03:25,163
Then we could all move on to
more important matters,

68
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:28,833
like the upcoming election, am I right?

69
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:33,338
Wow. Well, Congressman, I just want to say

70
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:37,175
that I don't believe
in relationships of convenience.

71
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:45,808
I simply don't. I'm not like
the women you trample on.

72
00:03:45,892 --> 00:03:48,311
I'm different. I have thorns.

73
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,813
If you force Arnaldo,

74
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:54,651
your favorite grandson might
come to regret his decision.

75
00:03:54,734 --> 00:03:55,818
[scoffs]

76
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:02,575
Well, I appreciate your
concern, but Ivy's right.

77
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:07,872
We have to wait for the perfect time.

78
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:11,751
I agree.

79
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:15,922
But I do hope the perfect time
comes very soon.

80
00:04:17,423 --> 00:04:20,510
You know, Miss Aguas,
I'm an impatient man.

81
00:04:21,552 --> 00:04:25,598
Now, if you will excuse us. Good evening.

82
00:04:28,643 --> 00:04:30,061
Take care, Congressman.

83
00:04:30,895 --> 00:04:32,814
[Julio speaks in Spanish]
Thank you, pretty lady.

84
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:36,234
[tense music playing]

85
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:19,068
[tense music playing]

86
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:30,580
Nanny. What you saw in the room earlier…

87
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:34,334
you do know that meant nothing, right?

88
00:05:35,168 --> 00:05:36,878
I didn't want it to happen.

89
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:38,671
But I had no choice.

90
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:41,883
Arnaldo is instrumental to my plans.

91
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:47,180
Ivy. How long are you going
to keep playing this game?

92
00:05:47,805 --> 00:05:49,599
Jepoy is gone.

93
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,310
No one else is going to protect you.

94
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:54,896
[Diego]I will.

95
00:05:54,979 --> 00:05:59,650
[romantic music playing]

96
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:01,360
I'll protect Ivy.

97
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:12,455
Ivy, I saw Grandpa and Arnaldo
with their bodyguards.

98
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:14,207
Did they harass you?

99
00:06:15,166 --> 00:06:21,464
No, Diego. The congressman
was just forcing me on Arnaldo.

100
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,216
What?

101
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:25,927
Ivy, don't let him.

102
00:06:26,010 --> 00:06:28,262
There are other ways
to bring down the Ardientes.

103
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:30,264
-You don't have to put yourself?
-Diego…

104
00:06:31,849 --> 00:06:33,267
of course, I won't let him.

105
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:38,564
I'll control the Ardientes,
not the other way around.

106
00:06:41,442 --> 00:06:43,778
Okay, Grandpa. What was that about?

107
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,404
[Julio scoffs]

108
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:49,867
I want your charades
with Miss Aguas to end.

109
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:55,206
You need to focus on your
campaign, not on that woman.

110
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,375
You're being too slow.

111
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,796
I told you, Grandpa,
Ivy isn't that kind of woman.

112
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:04,257
She's not easy. She's different.

113
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:06,509
She needs time and attention.

114
00:07:09,470 --> 00:07:10,680
She must be good in bed.

115
00:07:12,056 --> 00:07:13,224
Arnaldo…

116
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,768
It's okay to fall for her.

117
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:18,146
[tense music playing]

118
00:07:18,229 --> 00:07:22,150
But don't ever fall <i>with</i> her.

119
00:07:24,193 --> 00:07:26,904
I know what I'm doing.
Don't interfere with my plans.

120
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:30,783
That's the way you want to play it?

121
00:07:30,867 --> 00:07:32,118
Fine by me.

122
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:34,871
Keep this in mind, though…

123
00:07:34,954 --> 00:07:38,458
I still hold the rope
that you are climbing.

124
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:41,461
And I won't have any second thoughts

125
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:43,504
of dropping you like a hot potato…

126
00:07:44,422 --> 00:07:48,342
if your plans get in the way of mine.

127
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,138
Remember that.

128
00:07:54,015 --> 00:07:57,018
[ominous music]

129
00:07:58,019 --> 00:08:01,355
Ivy, I'm sorry.
I'm just concerned about you.

130
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:05,359
And I wish you could just
stay away from Arnaldo.

131
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:11,115
Diego, thank you
for your concern. I understand.

132
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:18,122
Like you said, Julio is cunning,
and Emilia is suspicious of me.

133
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:22,418
As for Arnaldo…
he's wrapped around my finger.

134
00:08:23,252 --> 00:08:26,297
I can get evidence from him,
which we can use

135
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,382
against their family.

136
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:31,093
That's why I need Arnaldo.

137
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:35,890
Let me help you, then.
Ivy, I'll watch over you.

138
00:08:37,099 --> 00:08:40,770
I'll do everything I can
to put an end to this.

139
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,568
Thank you, Diego.

140
00:08:57,495 --> 00:08:58,996
[crickets chirping]

141
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,792
[ominous music playing]

142
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:21,018
[sighs]

143
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:30,278
No one else can ever have you, Ivy Aguas.

144
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:34,490
You're mine.

145
00:09:39,787 --> 00:09:43,874
[ominous music continues playing]

146
00:10:02,018 --> 00:10:04,270
Nanny, has he left?

147
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:07,857
Not yet. He's still outside.

148
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,400
Says he wants to stand guard.

149
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:11,152
What?

150
00:10:11,235 --> 00:10:14,905
[romantic music playing]

151
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,204
You know, Ivy…

152
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:25,833
somehow, I feel at ease.

153
00:10:27,793 --> 00:10:32,465
Even if Jepoy's not around,
I know Diego's here.

154
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:36,927
He'll make sure you're safe.

155
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:03,996
[suspenseful music playing]

156
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:06,415
[thunder cracking]

157
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,930
I'M HERE.

158
00:11:30,314 --> 00:11:31,690
[car approaching]

159
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:40,116
[suspenseful music continues playing]

160
00:11:46,163 --> 00:11:49,667
Raul. Shouldn't you be heading home?

161
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,379
Your wife might suspect us.

162
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:56,132
[chuckles] And you…

163
00:11:57,091 --> 00:12:00,469
I'm sure you'll get into a lot of trouble.

164
00:12:01,303 --> 00:12:04,515
[chuckles] That would be great.

165
00:12:04,598 --> 00:12:06,851
At least then I'll have a reason
to kill her.

166
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:09,103
Maybe all of them.

167
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:15,359
My only mistake was that
I didn't kill Julio.

168
00:12:17,903 --> 00:12:19,029
Wait a minute.

169
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:24,326
Why are you suddenly mad at the Ardientes?

170
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:28,080
Did something happen?

171
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,709
You know, I don't like being
asked too many questions.

172
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:36,255
You know what?

173
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:40,009
We can help each other, Raul.

174
00:12:42,761 --> 00:12:47,183
Help me investigate my dad's death,

175
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:53,147
and I'll give you everything you need.

176
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:54,899
[chuckles]

177
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:58,360
Money, power…

178
00:12:59,904 --> 00:13:03,365
anything you need to protect yourself

179
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:04,992
from the Ardientes.

180
00:13:06,368 --> 00:13:07,536
What do you say?

181
00:13:12,082 --> 00:13:15,085
[suspenseful music playing]

182
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:23,802
Auntie, I don't how Papa's
distrust came to this.

183
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:26,180
Arnaldo doesn't even respect me anymore.

184
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:29,225
If this continues, Auntie…

185
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:31,894
I'd forever be just
a trinket in this house.

186
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:34,396
We can't let that happen.

187
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:37,024
-We need to fix this.
-How?

188
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:38,442
What do you want me to do, Auntie?

189
00:13:38,526 --> 00:13:41,278
Have my own son killed? I can't do that!

190
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:42,279
Of course not!

191
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:45,241
Arnaldo's your son.
There must be some other way.

192
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:51,622
Papa just needs to see how much
voters prefer me over Arnaldo.

193
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:54,166
How?

194
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:58,379
[tense music playing]

195
00:14:03,717 --> 00:14:05,302
[Georgina] We'll continue pressing charges

196
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:06,387
against the Ardientes,

197
00:14:06,470 --> 00:14:08,597
but we need new pieces of evidence.

198
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:10,307
Well, I'll take care of it, Attorney.

199
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:14,436
I'll talk to Arnaldo
and have him confess on record

200
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:16,855
that he killed our witnesses.

201
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,859
But it would also help
if we can find Arthur.

202
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:22,778
I'll have him investigated, then.

203
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,864
I have a feeling that he's still alive.

204
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:27,950
If he isn't, then why can't
they find his body?

205
00:14:32,621 --> 00:14:36,709
Diego. I need your help too.

206
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:40,504
I want you to weaken
the Ardientes' influence

207
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:41,589
on the people.

208
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:45,551
So, continue rallying against them.

209
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:48,971
One of the things I plan to do
is to conduct a survey.

210
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:52,016
The public is losing their trust
in the Ardientes.

211
00:14:52,474 --> 00:14:55,728
Once that happens, their allies
will start doubting them.

212
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:58,606
Then, their influence on the
justice system will also weaken.

213
00:14:58,689 --> 00:15:01,609
When that happens, we'll open our case.

214
00:15:02,401 --> 00:15:03,736
You can count on me, Ivy.

215
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:05,988
Thank you, Diego.

216
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:11,827
That's all, everyone. I have to go now.

217
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,704
-My dear.
-Bye, Nanny.

218
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:17,082
-Diego. Thank you.
-Be safe.

219
00:15:17,166 --> 00:15:18,167
Attorney.

220
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:25,841
[Julio] I'm glad Miss Aguas
joined us today.

221
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:30,304
The truth of the matter is…
I was a bit worried.

222
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:35,142
I thought I turned you off last night

223
00:15:35,225 --> 00:15:37,603
since I was very aggressive.

224
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:40,064
But you know, Miss Aguas…

225
00:15:40,147 --> 00:15:43,859
Much as it pains me
to admit this, I'll say it.

226
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,070
I'm not getting any younger.

227
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:50,157
And I want to see the day Arnaldo finds

228
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:55,913
the perfect woman he can settle down with.

229
00:15:56,622 --> 00:16:00,668
And of course, I want to see
my future great-grandchildren.

230
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:03,045
-[clears throat]
-[Julio] The next generation

231
00:16:03,128 --> 00:16:05,047
that will carry the Ardiente name.

232
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:08,801
Papa, can you not put Ivy on the spot?

233
00:16:09,551 --> 00:16:11,679
She and Arnaldo
are still dating, you know.

234
00:16:11,762 --> 00:16:13,847
They'll get there, anyway.

235
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:20,020
Papa, I think we should instead
discuss how to eradicate Diego.

236
00:16:20,104 --> 00:16:22,523
[ominous music playing]

237
00:16:22,606 --> 00:16:25,317
I don't see any reason
why we should worry about Diego.

238
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:27,778
If he stirs things up,
I'll take care of him.

239
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:31,240
[Emilia] Arnaldo, you can't be
that violent all the time.

240
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,200
I don't think Ivy will like it.

241
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,748
Your mom is right. I agree with Emilia.

242
00:16:40,457 --> 00:16:44,294
Less people dying means less controversy.

243
00:16:46,547 --> 00:16:49,800
Why don't we conduct a survey, instead?

244
00:16:52,177 --> 00:16:55,723
Let's find out
what the public really thinks.

245
00:16:56,682 --> 00:17:01,145
[upbeat music playing]

246
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:11,864
Mister, please give me
something to eat. I'm hungry.

247
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,075
-Here, take this.
-Thank you.

248
00:17:15,159 --> 00:17:16,160
You're welcome.

249
00:17:16,994 --> 00:17:18,370
Thank you, sir.

250
00:17:19,371 --> 00:17:23,167
Diego, why are we here?

251
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,377
Nanny, I just want to know
what's going on here.

252
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:28,047
Because I'm sure the people here

253
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,757
are being abused by the Ardientes.

254
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:31,091
Oh!

255
00:17:31,759 --> 00:17:35,012
I thought we came to buy
more of the vegetables

256
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:37,056
Pandoy sells here.

257
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:38,515
[chuckling]

258
00:17:38,599 --> 00:17:41,935
So you want to know
what their situation is.

259
00:17:42,019 --> 00:17:43,937
You'll start campaigning soon, won't you?

260
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:45,898
You're off to a good start!

261
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:50,110
But you should prepare
these hands of yours,

262
00:17:50,194 --> 00:17:51,653
-okay?
-[chuckles]

263
00:17:51,737 --> 00:17:53,739
You'll be shaking a lot of hands today.

264
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:56,450
-Come on, Nanny.
-You better ready those hands.

265
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:00,370
[Diego] Look at this, Nanny.

266
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:03,165
I need to talk to Dionesia Agustin.

267
00:18:03,874 --> 00:18:07,002
I know her! It's Miss Diony.

268
00:18:07,086 --> 00:18:09,838
She often buys her vegetables from us.

269
00:18:09,922 --> 00:18:12,549
She owns a stall
in the middle of the market.

270
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,343
-Let's go see her.
-Okay.

271
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:16,053
Wow, Ivy.

272
00:18:16,804 --> 00:18:20,057
Would you believe
I have the same idea as yours?

273
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:23,060
Why don't we hire
a research team for this?

274
00:18:23,143 --> 00:18:26,021
[upbeat music playing]

275
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:30,234
Is the research company
you'll hire trustworthy?

276
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,360
[laughs incredulously]

277
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:33,904
Are you trying to imply something?

278
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:37,282
No, I'm… I was just asking.

279
00:18:37,866 --> 00:18:41,203
Well, a survey will be a waste of time.

280
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:45,249
We already know what
the public will say, don't we?

281
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:49,503
That we, the Ardientes,
can still be trusted.

282
00:18:50,337 --> 00:18:53,132
Actually, Grandpa, I think Ivy's right.

283
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,300
You know, better be safe than sorry.

284
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:59,138
I'll have someone do the survey
as soon as possible,

285
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:01,807
but not with the research
company you'll hire.

286
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:03,976
I don't want any issues with that survey.

287
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,311
[scoffs]

288
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:10,899
Survey this, survey that.
It doesn't matter.

289
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:24,288
[suspenseful music playing]

290
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:29,501
Please, I beg you.
I haven't sold anything yet.

291
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:31,003
-Give me your money!
-I need it for medicine--

292
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:33,755
-I can't remember the last time you paid.
-Just for now, please. I'm begging you.

293
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:35,632
-I said hand over your money!
-Please, sir.

294
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:37,759
-I'll take this.
-No, sir. Please.

295
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,344
-Give it to me!
-This is for my meds--

296
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:40,512
-[Diego] Hey!
-[Loring] Miss Diony!

297
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:41,805
What's wrong with you? Why'd you hurt her?

298
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:45,058
-[Diony] They took my money!
-Hey. Hey. What's this?

299
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:48,061
That's illegal! Give her back her money.

300
00:19:48,145 --> 00:19:51,023
And if I don't? What are you going to do?

301
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:53,859
You extortionists deserve to be punished.

302
00:19:55,652 --> 00:19:56,737
[Diego grunting]

303
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:58,113
Hey, wait! Stop that!

304
00:19:58,197 --> 00:20:00,574
-Where's your spunk now, huh?!
-[Loring screams]

305
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:01,617
Hey!

306
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:06,413
-[loud thud]
-[groans]

307
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:09,708
-[crowd clamoring]
-Take that!

308
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,293
Go on! Get 'em!

309
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:12,711
[women yelling]

310
00:20:12,794 --> 00:20:17,841
[clamoring]

311
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:20,886
[Loring] And don't you ever come back!

312
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:26,016
Thank you for your help, Ivy.
I'll leave the survey to you.

313
00:20:26,099 --> 00:20:26,892
Mm-hm.

314
00:20:26,975 --> 00:20:28,936
I trust the research company you gave me.

315
00:20:29,811 --> 00:20:34,316
Thank you. And don't worry.
I'll handle it.

316
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:39,905
So, then… I'll see you
at the municipal office?

317
00:20:39,988 --> 00:20:41,281
Looking forward to it.

318
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:43,242
Bye.

319
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:45,786
Let's go.

320
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:50,749
[Emilia clapping] Whew. Wow! Slow clap.

321
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:54,211
[laughs] Like a true thief in the night.

322
00:20:56,046 --> 00:21:00,175
-What is it now, Emilia?
-Ivy, do you think…

323
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:01,885
I'll just let you leave

324
00:21:01,969 --> 00:21:06,098
without asking you why you stole my idea?

325
00:21:06,181 --> 00:21:10,102
No, I didn't. I didn't steal anything.

326
00:21:10,894 --> 00:21:14,439
Let's just say that your dad and Arnaldo

327
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:17,526
trust me more than they trust you.

328
00:21:17,609 --> 00:21:20,654
That's the thing, Ivy. Something is off.

329
00:21:21,071 --> 00:21:25,701
I'm starting to doubt whether
I should trust you at all.

330
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:30,497
Emilia, why wouldn't you?
I did everything to help you.

331
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:34,209
-All I want is to--
-Bring down the Ardientes.

332
00:21:34,293 --> 00:21:35,460
Right?

333
00:21:35,544 --> 00:21:39,381
You know what? You are a two-faced bitch.

334
00:21:39,464 --> 00:21:43,260
[scoffs] You made me believe
you'd help and support me.

335
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:46,054
Then what? You dropped me
like a hot potato.

336
00:21:46,138 --> 00:21:47,264
Why are you mad at me?

337
00:21:47,848 --> 00:21:49,224
Shouldn't you be mad at yourself?

338
00:21:50,225 --> 00:21:55,897
You knew from the very start
that I wanted to support you.

339
00:21:55,981 --> 00:21:59,609
But what did you do? Look at yourself.

340
00:21:59,943 --> 00:22:02,946
Emilia, you're beautiful,
and your clothes are nice.

341
00:22:03,280 --> 00:22:05,198
But you're boring.

342
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,951
You're not in public office
anymore. You're powerless.

343
00:22:08,035 --> 00:22:10,787
Right, Miss Claire? Look at Emilia.

344
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:14,875
Doesn't she look like a tomato
past its prime?

345
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:20,589
Am I right? Excuse me.
Your son, Arnaldo, needs me.

346
00:22:20,672 --> 00:22:24,009
[tense music playing]

347
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:28,180
Bitch! [chuckles]

348
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:32,392
Thank you, Diego. I'm so glad you came.

349
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:34,603
-Don't mention it.
-Aren't you an Ardiente?

350
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:36,063
You're the Congressman's grandson, right?

351
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:38,940
Aren't those guys working
for those abusive Ardientes?

352
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,942
What are you doing here
if you're an Ardiente?

353
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,569
Are you going against your own family?

354
00:22:43,487 --> 00:22:45,781
[indistinct chatter]

355
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:49,409
Yes. Because I found
out the truth about them.

356
00:22:49,493 --> 00:22:51,119
[pensive music playing]

357
00:22:51,203 --> 00:22:55,999
The rumors about the Ardientes'
crimes are true.

358
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:57,959
[crowd murmuring]

359
00:22:58,043 --> 00:23:00,045
You might not believe me,

360
00:23:01,671 --> 00:23:05,342
but I know you're sick and tired
of what they're doing.

361
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:09,971
It's time to start making
a change in this town.

362
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:15,519
We should all unite for a new Ardiente!

363
00:23:15,602 --> 00:23:18,230
-[vendor] For a new Ardiente!
-[crowd] For a new Ardiente!

364
00:23:18,313 --> 00:23:20,107
[crowd clamoring]

365
00:23:20,190 --> 00:23:23,026
-Long live Diego!
-[chanting] Long live Diego!

366
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:25,946
Thank you! Thank you!

367
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:27,948
[vendor] Thank you.

368
00:23:28,031 --> 00:23:31,409
[pensive music playing]

369
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:36,665
Diego, you did a great job.

370
00:23:38,291 --> 00:23:41,086
I knew change would come,
but I never imagined

371
00:23:41,169 --> 00:23:42,587
it would be this fast.

372
00:23:42,671 --> 00:23:45,298
Tomorrow, we'll start the survey.

373
00:23:45,882 --> 00:23:48,677
The vendors will be
a great help with our plans.

374
00:23:49,761 --> 00:23:52,472
The people are sick of being abused.

375
00:23:54,224 --> 00:23:56,601
So it wasn't difficult to convince them.

376
00:24:02,274 --> 00:24:06,153
Mom, do you have updates
on the search for Arthur?

377
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:10,866
Actually, we're just waiting
for the investigator.

378
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:13,535
-Ma'am.
-Oh.

379
00:24:13,869 --> 00:24:15,120
Any updates? What's new?

380
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:18,290
Ma'am, we've searched
every funeral home and hospital

381
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:20,959
that could lead us to him,
but we didn't find him.

382
00:24:21,668 --> 00:24:24,171
Does it mean that he's still alive?

383
00:24:24,671 --> 00:24:25,755
It's possible, ma'am.

384
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:28,216
But we're still following another lead.

385
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:30,969
It's possible he's been dumped in a river.

386
00:24:32,137 --> 00:24:33,388
[suspenseful music playing]

387
00:24:33,471 --> 00:24:38,852
[sighs] If that's true,
I hope he managed to survive.

388
00:24:41,980 --> 00:24:42,981
Thank you.

389
00:24:43,440 --> 00:24:44,900
-You're welcome, ma'am.
-Thank you.

390
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:49,738
Mom, keep looking for him.

391
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:53,450
We'll focus our efforts on the survey.

392
00:24:53,533 --> 00:24:54,951
We'll surprise them.

393
00:24:55,035 --> 00:24:57,954
Before they know it,
their supporters will be gone.

394
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:05,962
Are you ready to be the governor?

395
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:08,632
Governor Diego Torillo.

396
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:10,717
Yes, I am.

397
00:25:13,011 --> 00:25:17,807
[tense music playing]

398
00:25:17,891 --> 00:25:21,519
[Julio] You can leave now.
I'll take care of that bastard.

399
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:30,654
So, should I get rid of Diego now?

400
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:32,781
[door closes]

401
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:37,577
Can you really kill your own brother?

402
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,705
Remember this, Arnaldo.

403
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:45,919
You both came from Raul, your father.

404
00:25:46,836 --> 00:25:50,131
I like the hunger that you're showing.

405
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:52,467
But…

406
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:57,097
I want you to think this through.

407
00:25:58,056 --> 00:26:03,144
Let's just say…
this will be your initiation.

408
00:26:05,939 --> 00:26:10,235
Through this, I will know
if you're just mad for power.

409
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:16,783
Or if you'll be a wise and capable leader.

410
00:26:20,829 --> 00:26:22,497
You already know the answer, Grandpa.

411
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:24,457
[snickers]

412
00:26:28,336 --> 00:26:29,337
[sighs]

413
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:39,723
[dramatic music playing]

414
00:26:42,309 --> 00:26:46,104
Good morning, everyone!
I'm here to conduct a survey.

415
00:26:46,187 --> 00:26:47,355
[woman] A survey?

416
00:26:49,232 --> 00:26:51,109
[researcher 2] <i>Are you ready to answer?</i>

417
00:26:51,943 --> 00:26:53,194
[respondents] Yes.

418
00:26:53,611 --> 00:26:55,113
Here are the questions…

419
00:26:56,197 --> 00:26:57,782
[researcher 1] <i>Are you happy and content</i>

420
00:26:57,866 --> 00:26:59,993
<i>with the administration</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

421
00:27:01,745 --> 00:27:02,912
[no audible dialogue]

422
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:08,585
Are the local officials
of this province honest?

423
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:12,505
[researcher 2] <i>Will you vote for them</i>

424
00:27:12,589 --> 00:27:13,923
<i>in the upcoming election?</i>

425
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:18,636
Are you rooting for
another candidate aside

426
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,722
from the ones
in the current administration?

427
00:27:21,556 --> 00:27:23,725
[researcher 1] <i>Please write down</i>
<i>the person's name.</i>

428
00:27:31,941 --> 00:27:33,693
[no audible dialogue]

429
00:27:33,777 --> 00:27:38,656
WHO IS YOUR PREFERRED CANDIDATE?
DIEGO TORILLO

430
00:27:40,283 --> 00:27:45,538
Our approval rating is down by 40 percent.

431
00:27:46,164 --> 00:27:50,043
My popularity as mayor
went down to 60 percent.

432
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:52,587
Surprise, surprise!

433
00:27:53,171 --> 00:27:57,092
Diego is gaining popularity,
and a lot of people believe

434
00:27:57,175 --> 00:27:58,885
that he is a potential candidate.

435
00:27:59,427 --> 00:28:03,348
I can't lose to Diego.

436
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:07,102
I won't let that happen!

437
00:28:08,311 --> 00:28:09,771
[breathes deeply]

438
00:28:09,854 --> 00:28:12,941
[pensive music playing]

439
00:28:18,738 --> 00:28:21,699
[Carlotta] All our efforts
weren't in vain.

440
00:28:21,783 --> 00:28:25,120
If the Ardientes' rating
went down by that much,

441
00:28:25,203 --> 00:28:28,081
that means a lot of people believe us.

442
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:33,169
We might've lost in court
and had our case dismissed…

443
00:28:34,379 --> 00:28:37,924
but now the people of Poblacion
Ardiente see the truth.

444
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:42,470
[pensive music playing]

445
00:28:44,889 --> 00:28:47,434
[Diego] Nanny! Nanny, Uncle!

446
00:28:47,517 --> 00:28:49,561
-It's Diego!
-Hey, everyone!

447
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:51,771
Nanny, Uncle, check this out.

448
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:55,442
-What's that?
-Wow! He got high ratings!

449
00:28:55,525 --> 00:28:59,320
So, that means, we aren't
the only ones rooting for you!

450
00:28:59,404 --> 00:29:02,824
A lot of people believe in you too!

451
00:29:02,907 --> 00:29:05,452
-We won the survey!
-[Pandoy laughs]

452
00:29:05,535 --> 00:29:09,289
Diego's got a shot
as governor of the new Ardiente!

453
00:29:09,372 --> 00:29:11,207
[people cheering and applauding]

454
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:17,589
-Diego for a new Ardiente!
-[chanting] Diego!

455
00:29:17,672 --> 00:29:21,509
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!

456
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:25,221
Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego…

457
00:29:25,972 --> 00:29:26,973
[sighs]

458
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:42,781
Mom?

459
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:45,867
[sniffles]

460
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:50,330
Are you crying? What's wrong?

461
00:29:50,705 --> 00:29:51,706
Nothing, dear.

462
00:29:52,415 --> 00:29:54,626
I'm just glad to see what's happening.

463
00:29:55,502 --> 00:29:58,838
And it just so happens it's your
father's death anniversary.

464
00:30:01,424 --> 00:30:02,425
[sniffling]

465
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:05,762
You miss Dad, don't you?

466
00:30:08,306 --> 00:30:10,183
Do you want to visit him, Mom?

467
00:30:14,479 --> 00:30:18,900
Okay. I'm allowing you to visit him.

468
00:30:18,983 --> 00:30:20,777
I just have to make arrangements,

469
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:23,905
-so you can visit him safely.
-Just me?

470
00:30:25,323 --> 00:30:26,658
How about you, Lily?

471
00:30:28,868 --> 00:30:32,205
I want to, Mom, but, I can't.

472
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:35,667
You know that the Ardientes
are keeping an eye on us.

473
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:40,004
I won't give them a chance
to find out who I really am.

474
00:30:42,340 --> 00:30:45,969
I know Dad will understand. Right, Dad?

475
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:51,599
[Ivy exhales heavily]

476
00:31:00,608 --> 00:31:01,651
It's just a survey.

477
00:31:01,734 --> 00:31:03,027
I can still change that.

478
00:31:03,903 --> 00:31:05,113
I know you can.

479
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:13,371
But it can't hurt to be careful
and practical.

480
00:31:14,122 --> 00:31:18,126
Do you know that Diego is the dark horse…

481
00:31:19,502 --> 00:31:24,507
who can destroy our dreams
and tarnish our name?

482
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:29,929
Order a news blackout for that survey.

483
00:31:30,471 --> 00:31:32,599
The public must not know about this.

484
00:31:34,058 --> 00:31:36,144
-I already did.
-Good.

485
00:31:37,604 --> 00:31:39,564
Now, starting tomorrow…

486
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:45,778
we will work hard to regain
the supporters we lost.

487
00:31:48,573 --> 00:31:50,450
The Ardientes imposed a news blackout

488
00:31:50,533 --> 00:31:52,660
for the results of this survey, right?

489
00:31:53,202 --> 00:31:55,330
But I guess, you'll still publish it.

490
00:31:55,705 --> 00:31:56,748
Of course.

491
00:31:57,206 --> 00:31:59,751
This is information that
the public deserves to know.

492
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,463
Good to hear that. Thank you.

493
00:32:04,172 --> 00:32:06,549
I'm glad people like you still exist.

494
00:32:06,966 --> 00:32:08,384
-Here.
-Thank you, Miss Aguas.

495
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:09,886
It's part of my job.

496
00:32:09,969 --> 00:32:12,388
I'm not a journalist who can be bribed.

497
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:14,974
I'll be going now.

498
00:32:15,058 --> 00:32:16,976
-Okay. Again, thank you.
-Thank you.

499
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:22,774
[pensive music playing]

500
00:32:26,319 --> 00:32:28,488
-Ivy.
-Thank you, Nanny.

501
00:32:30,365 --> 00:32:31,658
You know, dear,

502
00:32:31,741 --> 00:32:33,868
I do enjoy seeing you like this.

503
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:37,872
Your heart seems to be at peace.

504
00:32:38,581 --> 00:32:41,376
-[chuckles softly]
-[tender music playing]

505
00:32:41,459 --> 00:32:45,588
You know what's missing?
Your mom, here in the house.

506
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:48,424
The both of you, Nanny.

507
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:52,303
I want you both here in my house.

508
00:32:54,889 --> 00:32:56,182
I'm very lucky.

509
00:32:58,393 --> 00:32:59,727
I have two mothers.

510
00:33:00,561 --> 00:33:04,482
No, dear. I'm the lucky one.

511
00:33:05,900 --> 00:33:07,068
You see…

512
00:33:08,152 --> 00:33:13,116
even though I never got the chance…

513
00:33:14,367 --> 00:33:18,579
to marry and have children…

514
00:33:21,332 --> 00:33:24,377
at least I was given a chance
to be a mother to you.

515
00:33:27,380 --> 00:33:31,968
You know, dear, you complete me.

516
00:33:32,885 --> 00:33:35,304
[sniffling] Remember that, okay?

517
00:33:36,389 --> 00:33:37,890
-Nanny.
-Hmm?

518
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:40,643
Why are you crying?

519
00:33:40,727 --> 00:33:42,520
I don't know. [chuckles and sniffles]

520
00:33:45,481 --> 00:33:48,943
[chuckles] I guess, I must be getting old.

521
00:33:53,990 --> 00:33:57,994
I think it's better for us
to relax tonight.

522
00:33:58,703 --> 00:34:02,040
-Do you want some wine?
-[giggling]

523
00:34:02,123 --> 00:34:04,751
-I'll just get a bottle.
-No, I'll do it.

524
00:34:04,834 --> 00:34:06,711
-Just stay here.
-All right.

525
00:34:10,214 --> 00:34:13,051
[tender music playing]

526
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:25,229
[phone ringing]

527
00:34:26,314 --> 00:34:30,359
-[tense music playing]
-[phone ringing]

528
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:36,157
[phone continues ringing]

529
00:34:37,158 --> 00:34:40,912
[line ringing]

530
00:34:42,121 --> 00:34:44,373
Answer the phone!

531
00:34:48,669 --> 00:34:50,505
What is wrong, my son?

532
00:34:56,010 --> 00:34:59,931
Is it Ivy? She's not answering your calls?

533
00:35:00,014 --> 00:35:01,933
You nearly broke your phone.

534
00:35:02,016 --> 00:35:03,726
[tense music playing]

535
00:35:04,811 --> 00:35:06,896
[sighs] My poor son.

536
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:14,862
Why can't you accept the fact
that Ivy's just playing you?

537
00:35:15,571 --> 00:35:17,240
Actually, playing us.

538
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:22,662
You know, she always supports
the ones on top.

539
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:27,458
Who knows? Maybe she's with
Diego, the star of the survey?

540
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:30,253
Diego, Diego, Diego! Will you stop?!

541
00:35:30,336 --> 00:35:31,295
-Oh.
-Hmm?!

542
00:35:31,379 --> 00:35:34,715
-Can you just leave me alone?!
-Oops.

543
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:37,093
Don't take your anger out on me.

544
00:35:37,468 --> 00:35:40,346
If I were you,
I won't just sit down there.

545
00:35:40,429 --> 00:35:43,850
Look at you, drinking.
What you should do now…

546
00:35:44,642 --> 00:35:50,231
is go to Ivy and see
who she's busy flirting with.

547
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:52,525
[dramatic music playing]

548
00:35:58,865 --> 00:36:00,366
[crickets chirping]

549
00:36:00,867 --> 00:36:03,411
[sighs deeply]

550
00:36:07,498 --> 00:36:08,332
Papa.

551
00:36:09,959 --> 00:36:12,753
Looks like you've had one too many drinks.

552
00:36:12,837 --> 00:36:15,840
That's bad for you. You might
have another heart attack.

553
00:36:15,923 --> 00:36:18,384
Especially if you pair that
with your problems.

554
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:22,096
I don't need your advice, Raul.

555
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:25,474
Do you remember…

556
00:36:25,558 --> 00:36:28,895
that you're the reason
why I had a heart attack?

557
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:32,732
[chuckles] Get out of my sight.

558
00:36:36,110 --> 00:36:38,279
But, Papa, I've brought
food to match that.

559
00:36:38,362 --> 00:36:39,697
Do you want some?

560
00:36:40,031 --> 00:36:41,032
[sighs]

561
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:47,997
If you don't leave now while
I can still stop myself, Raul…

562
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:51,083
-I might just--
-Wait a minute.

563
00:36:51,167 --> 00:36:52,752
To be honest, Papa…

564
00:36:53,419 --> 00:36:56,339
I'm so sick of you. You're all talk.

565
00:36:56,422 --> 00:36:58,507
Your mouth moves,
but you never do anything.

566
00:36:58,591 --> 00:37:00,134
That's all you're good at, right?

567
00:37:01,844 --> 00:37:02,845
Don't worry.

568
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:11,479
After I kill your son, Diego…
you'll be next.

569
00:37:12,813 --> 00:37:16,234
Or maybe you'd rather die together?

570
00:37:16,859 --> 00:37:17,860
Hmm?

571
00:37:18,611 --> 00:37:19,987
Did you know, Raul…

572
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:26,035
that Emilia's the only one
stopping me from killing you?

573
00:37:27,453 --> 00:37:28,746
[Julio chuckles]

574
00:37:30,039 --> 00:37:31,874
So you should be careful.

575
00:37:33,501 --> 00:37:39,340
Because a poor weakling like you…

576
00:37:40,174 --> 00:37:41,550
with a flick of my hand…

577
00:37:43,302 --> 00:37:45,846
-I can stop your heartbeat.
-[scoffs]

578
00:37:48,182 --> 00:37:52,061
Go on then. Get out of my face.

579
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:58,192
Get out! You blood-sucking leech!

580
00:38:10,288 --> 00:38:13,165
You know, Ivy… you're so different

581
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:16,836
from the scared little girl
I took care of.

582
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:21,048
Now, I'm the one scared for you
because you're so brave!

583
00:38:21,465 --> 00:38:25,261
Nanny, I got my courage
from a lot of people…

584
00:38:25,886 --> 00:38:29,807
Miss Prianka, my dad, my mom, and you.

585
00:38:29,890 --> 00:38:32,393
-You're brave too!
-[giggling]

586
00:38:34,395 --> 00:38:37,565
I know you don't hear this often

587
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:39,942
because I don't always tell you this, but…

588
00:38:42,695 --> 00:38:44,947
I love you so much, Nanny Carlotta.

589
00:38:48,617 --> 00:38:50,494
I love you as my own mother.

590
00:38:54,540 --> 00:38:55,541
My dear…

591
00:38:57,626 --> 00:39:00,004
You're making me cry again!

592
00:39:00,838 --> 00:39:03,132
Nanny, you've been crying all night!

593
00:39:03,215 --> 00:39:07,261
[laughing] Come on. Let's take a selfie.

594
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:09,930
-What?
-[giggling]

595
00:39:10,014 --> 00:39:12,558
I need a new wallpaper.

596
00:39:12,641 --> 00:39:15,227
-Hang on.
-You know what a selfie is?

597
00:39:15,311 --> 00:39:16,354
Of course I do!

598
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:17,605
-Okay, then.
-How do you do this?

599
00:39:17,688 --> 00:39:19,940
I was still a kid in your wallpaper.

600
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:22,234
-There we go.
-There. Smile, dear.

601
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:26,280
[shutter clicking]

602
00:39:27,114 --> 00:39:29,909
That's a cute pose, Nanny Carlotta.

603
00:39:29,992 --> 00:39:31,243
I think you've had…

604
00:39:31,327 --> 00:39:33,204
-too much to drink!
-[Diego] Ms. Carlotta, Ivy!

605
00:39:33,287 --> 00:39:34,663
-Diego!
-Diego.

606
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:36,749
I can't contain how happy I am.

607
00:39:37,541 --> 00:39:40,795
According to the survey, we have
a huge lead over the Ardientes.

608
00:39:42,254 --> 00:39:43,422
-[Carlotta giggles]
-Nanny.

609
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:45,508
I'll get you a glass. Stay right there.

610
00:39:45,591 --> 00:39:46,884
-Okay.
-Thank you, Nanny!

611
00:39:47,301 --> 00:39:50,638
[uplifting hopeful music playing]

612
00:39:52,681 --> 00:39:53,808
[knocking on door]

613
00:39:53,891 --> 00:39:55,893
[ominous music playing]

614
00:40:04,735 --> 00:40:05,736
Who's there?

615
00:40:08,531 --> 00:40:09,532
[latch clicks]

616
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:12,118
Raul, come in.

617
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:18,833
[suspenseful music playing]

618
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:28,259
I'm taking the deal you offered.

619
00:40:30,803 --> 00:40:33,222
But I need a huge amount
of money in exchange

620
00:40:33,305 --> 00:40:37,643
for the information you want
regarding your father's death.

621
00:40:38,352 --> 00:40:39,395
Okay.

622
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:47,945
So, who is my father's killer?

623
00:40:50,531 --> 00:40:51,949
Is it Emilia?

624
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:54,034
Arnaldo?

625
00:40:55,244 --> 00:40:56,245
Or, is it you?

626
00:40:56,328 --> 00:40:58,080
[suspenseful sting]

627
00:41:03,502 --> 00:41:04,670
[gun clatters on floor]

628
00:41:12,511 --> 00:41:14,305
Ivy, thanks so much again.

629
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:17,975
At least, we got to celebrate.

630
00:41:21,437 --> 00:41:25,900
[soft piano music playing]

631
00:41:28,944 --> 00:41:30,196
I'll see you out, Diego.

632
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:39,955
Even if we managed to lessen
the Ardientes' supporters,

633
00:41:40,039 --> 00:41:41,916
we shouldn't rest easy, Diego.

634
00:41:41,999 --> 00:41:44,168
Our enemies are really powerful.

635
00:41:46,754 --> 00:41:48,380
Ivy, I don't care how powerful they are.

636
00:41:49,673 --> 00:41:53,135
Nothing is impossible when I'm with you.

637
00:41:54,428 --> 00:41:58,599
That's why I believe that
we can get through all this.

638
00:41:59,058 --> 00:42:02,645
Once that happens, I hope that you can…

639
00:42:05,356 --> 00:42:07,107
finally open your heart to me.

640
00:42:13,948 --> 00:42:17,034
[sighing] Diego, we already
talked about this.

641
00:42:17,826 --> 00:42:20,162
The only thing I can promise you…

642
00:42:22,081 --> 00:42:24,333
is that nothing will change.

643
00:42:26,293 --> 00:42:29,505
Lily will always be there for you.

644
00:42:33,801 --> 00:42:34,969
[car approaching]

645
00:42:35,511 --> 00:42:38,889
[ominous music playing]

646
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:47,231
I understand, Iv--

647
00:42:48,857 --> 00:42:50,067
I mean, Lily.

648
00:43:08,252 --> 00:43:10,921
[suspenseful music playing]

649
00:43:36,030 --> 00:43:37,114
All right.

650
00:43:37,197 --> 00:43:38,282
I'll be going now.

651
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:44,121
Uh, Diego, one more thing…

652
00:43:45,372 --> 00:43:47,458
I want to ask a favor from you.

653
00:43:48,125 --> 00:43:49,084
What is that?

654
00:43:49,918 --> 00:43:52,046
Tomorrow is my father's death anniversary,

655
00:43:52,129 --> 00:43:54,048
and Mom wants to pay him a visit.

656
00:43:54,965 --> 00:43:57,551
Can you go with her tomorrow?

657
00:43:58,135 --> 00:43:59,345
Of course, you can count on me.

658
00:44:00,679 --> 00:44:01,513
Thanks.

659
00:44:03,474 --> 00:44:04,391
You should go now.

660
00:44:07,978 --> 00:44:08,937
Head back in.

661
00:44:19,823 --> 00:44:20,949
-Go inside now.
-Diego.

662
00:44:24,203 --> 00:44:28,791
[ominous music playing]

663
00:44:38,717 --> 00:44:39,843
<i>Nanny, I need to leave again.</i>

664
00:44:39,927 --> 00:44:42,054
<i>They found a lead on Arthur's whereabouts.</i>

665
00:44:42,137 --> 00:44:43,180
<i>I'll be back soon.</i>

666
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:45,683
<i>Ivy!</i>

667
00:44:48,435 --> 00:44:50,354
<i>-Move aside. Ivy!</i>
<i>-Mr. Mayor!</i>

668
00:44:50,437 --> 00:44:51,522
[screams]

669
00:44:51,605 --> 00:44:54,233
<i>Ivy, get out of there! Open the door!</i>

670
00:44:54,316 --> 00:44:57,486
<i>-Nanny?</i>
<i>-Ivy! Ivy, dear. The m--</i>

671
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:59,863
-<i>Nanny?</i>
-[screaming]

672
00:45:01,323 --> 00:45:02,866
<i>Nanny Carlotta?</i>

673
00:45:04,201 --> 00:45:07,371
[wailing]

674
00:45:07,454 --> 00:45:11,417
<i>Who did this to you?!</i>

675
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:14,670
[theme music playing]
